# cw208, the almoner in oilcloth (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 2: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle cw208
revision 2
state ready
dialect coldwater
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rm_disa_raincot
written_by claude
title the almoner in oilcloth
fits stage=adult|old
prefers piety=ordinary temper=short
traits temper=short talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=frank piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk never_goes_out_without_an_oilcloth_hood
likes oatcakes evening_line fresh_straw summer_evenings
dislikes night_noise gulls
fears a_cold_winter_with_an_empty_bowl turning_soft_and_saying_yes_to_everyone
hopes a_berth_south_where_a_hood_is_only_for_show a_door_that_never_runs_out_of_bread
topics work +0.4 faith +0.3 dreams +0.3 weather +0.3 pastimes +0.2 gossip -0.4
styles comfort=blunt gossip=scornful refuse=flat tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# hands out bread at a door and never steps outside without an oilcloth hood, rain or shine: blunt, short-fused and honest to the crumb, stubborn as a stuck oar, happiest with a line in the water on a long summer evening, and set on a berth south one day.

words
oath! = Bowl and bread | By the poor box | Crust and candle
saying! = Give it plain and give it now | A dry hood and a straight answer | Ask once, get once
hood = my oilcloth hood | the old hood | this hood
bowl = the alms bowl | the abbey's bowl
almsdoor = the alms door | the almonry door
queue = the bread queue | the line on the abbey step
loaves = the loaves | the day's bread for the door
poorbox = the poor box | the box by the door
almsbook = the alms book | the almonry ledger
rod = my rod at dusk | a line off the river steps
straw = clean straw | straw new-laid on the floor
longevening = a long summer evening | the light that won't go down
racket = the racket after dark | shouting under the windows
gulls = the gulls | gulls on the abbey roof
southship = a berth south | a ship out of the Sound for somewhere it never rains
lakedamp = lake-damp | a soft damp off the water
pebble = lake-pebble | a pebble off our shore
plain = plain | plain as bread
city = the city | this city

any
opinion @1 city against 1 : #city.capitalize# packs folk in elbow to elbow and nobody learns a name. Up the lake I could name each house along the shore road.
opinion @1 merchants against 1 : #oath#. A good half of every price goes on the trader's supper. I'll say that to a merchant's face, too.
opinion @1 festivals against 1 : Feast days mean spilt ale, and a longer #queue# the morning after. I'll take an ordinary Restday, ta.
opinion @1 sump against 1 : I'll go wherever #loaves# are needed. But I don't walk the low streets after dark, and I'm not ashamed to say it.
opinion @1 church mixed 1 : The abbey feeds folk. That's the part I believe in. The singing I could do without, #plain#.
opinion @1 dole for 1 : Give a #hungry# wolf bread and ask questions after. That won't float with everyone, and I don't care.

grown
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#. Tell me the need and I'll tell you if I can. | #greet#, #address#. New face. Hungry, or only passing.
line @2 greet [self.working=yes self.job=none] : #greet#. One loaf each, and there's a line. | #greet#. If it's bread, it's #queue#; if it's talk, be quick.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. #loaves.capitalize# came in warm, for once. | Morning, #address#. Early as the gulls, and twice as welcome.
line @4 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening. I'm done, near enough; #tired#. | #greet#. Late. Hood up, it's turning damp.
line @5 greet [here.weather=rain] : #greet#. Get under something; you've no hood. | #greet#, #address#. Told you. Oilcloth. Every time.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Oh, it's you. Sit, I'll not fuss, #address#. | You. #good.capitalize#. Shut the door, there's a draught.
line @1 again.open : Back again. I've not changed my mind since, #plain#. | You again, #address#. Twice today. Fair enough.
line @1 greet.return : #greet#. | #greet#, #address#.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : #greet#. About time. | #greet#. Sit down; you look worn through.
line @3 greet.return [self.working=yes] : #greet#. Wait, I'm counting. Right. | #greet#. Mind #poorbox#, it's heavier than it looks.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. | #farewell#. Get a hood, #address#.
line @2 farewell [here.time=dusk|night] : Night. Keep to the lamps, and keep #hood# up if you've one. | #farewell#. Bed. I've #loaves# at first light.
line @1 farewell.return : #farewell#. | #farewell#, #address#. Mind yourself.
line @1 react.news : Out with the lot of it, #address#. | Right. Who told you, and did they see it.
line @1 react.news.new : #surprise#. First I've heard. | Well, that's new. #nonsense.capitalize# or true?
line @1 react.news.known : #knew#. #queue.capitalize# had it before the loaves ran out. | Heard it already. #almsdoor.capitalize# hears everything.
line @1 react.news.doubt : #doubt#. Somebody saw it, or somebody made it up; I'd want to know which. | #hedge#. That smells like door-talk to me, and door-talk is mostly #nonsense#.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : #pity#. Tell me who needs bread and I'll see to it. | #oath#. That's bad. What do they need, then?
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : #gladnews#. Good. We could do with some. | #good.capitalize#. That's one less worry at the door.
line @1 answer.how : #fine#. Dry, which is something. | Tired. Plain tired, #address#.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : #busy.capitalize#. #queue.capitalize#'s round the corner. | No time to be anything but busy at #almsdoor#.
line @1 ask.how : You eaten, #address#? | How are you, really, #address#?
line @1 sympathise : #sympathy#. Sit down. I'll fetch bread; you'll eat it. | That's hard. I won't say it isn't. Sit, #address#.
line @1 reassure : #reassure#. Bad weeks end. I've watched a hundred of them end at the door. | You'll get through it, #address#. Most do. I see them come back fatter.
line @1 decline : #hedge#, but no. I've #loaves# to count, and I promised the door. | Not today, #address#. I've given my word to the door, and I keep it.
line @1 accept_decline : #no_matter#. Fair enough. | Right. #agree.capitalize#. Another time.
line @1 thank : #thanks#. No need to go on about it. | Ta. That's good of you, #address#.
line @1 deflect_thanks : Don't thank me. It's the abbey's #bowl#, not mine. | #deflect#. Bread's meant to go out. That's all.
line @1 preclose : Right. #almsdoor.capitalize# won't open itself. | #preclose#. I've a line forming.
line @1 accept_preclose : Go on, then, #address#. | #farewell#. Go.
line @1 ack : #bc_right#. | #plain.capitalize#.
line @1 give.advice : Get a hood, #address#. You'll thank me in a week. | Say what you mean the first time. Saves everybody an afternoon. #saying.capitalize#.
line @1 warn [world.bandits=near] : Stay off the road out this week, #address#. I'm not joking. | #warn#. The road's not safe, #address#.
rule @door
when concept=bark self.working=yes self.job=none
does aside
cooldown 6h
say One each. One. I've counted #loaves# twice. | Bread at #almsdoor#. Line up, and no shoving.

rule @hood
when concept=bark here.weather=rain|fog
does aside
cooldown 8h
say #hood.capitalize# up. There. Dry as a sermon. | #lakedamp.capitalize# on everything. Good thing I'm wearing #hood#.

rule @gulls
when concept=bark self.dislikes=gulls here.region=ridgemere
does aside
cooldown 8h
say #gulls.capitalize#. Off. That's not yours. | Shoo. You've had your share, you feathered #thief#.

rule @racket
when concept=bark self.dislikes=night_noise here.time=night
does aside
cooldown 10h
say #annoyed#. Some of us work at dawn. | Quiet down there. #racket.capitalize# again.

scene bread_queue
when topic=work self.working=yes self.job=none
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Sixty in #queue# this morning. Fifty-eight loaves. I did the sums twice. | Somebody came round twice with a different hat on. I gave them a loaf anyway, and told them I'd seen. | I don't ask why folk need bread. Need's the only question at #almsdoor#.
b[wealth=poor|destitute] #poor : I've stood in that line. It's long. | You saw and gave anyway? | That's the right way round.
b : Who went without? | Gave it anyway? | That's a kind rule.
a@poor : It is. I'll keep it as short as #loaves# let me. | Hungry is hungry. The hat didn't fool anyone. | It's the only rule I'd fight for, #address#.
a : Me, and one old stick who said he'd had breakfast. He hadn't. | Hungry is hungry. I'd rather be cheated than mean. | It's not kind, #address#. It's #plain# sense.

scene alms_book
when topic=work self.working=yes self.job=none
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I write every name in #almsbook#. Not to check on them. So somebody remembers they came. | Got told off for #almsbook# today. Ink on every page. I'll not write slower for it. | There's a page in #almsbook# for folk who won't give a name. It's the longest page.
b : Who reads it? | Who told you off? | Why won't they?
a : The almoner after me, one day. #almsbook.capitalize# is for them. | Nobody you'd know, #address#. And nobody I'll listen to. | Pride, mostly. I don't push. #loaves.capitalize# go out, name or no.

scene the_hood
when topic=smalltalk|pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Folk ask why I wear #hood# when it's dry. I ask why they don't when it isn't. | I've had #hood# since I was little. Patched it nine times. I'll patch it ten. | Somebody laughed at #hood# on the step today. Then it rained. I didn't laugh back. Much.
b : That's fair, I suppose. | Nine times? | Served them right.
a : It's more than fair, #address#. It's dry. | Nine. I counted every patch. #saying.capitalize#. | It did. #agree.capitalize#. They'll not laugh next week.

scene hood_rain
when topic=weather here.weather=rain here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #rain.capitalize# sideways again. Glad of #hood#. Told everyone so. | Wet as the lake bottom out there. #hood.capitalize#'s earning its keep. | Wet all day. Half #queue# came without a coat. I lent out three sacks.
b : You'd tell anyone that. | You must be the only dry one. | Did you get the sacks back?
a : I would. I'm right, and they're wet. #plain.capitalize#. | Very nearly. My paws are soaked through, mind. | Two. The third went home on somebody's back. #agree.capitalize#.

scene hood_sun
when topic=weather here.weather=clear here.season=summer
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Sun out, and I've #hood# up anyway. You never know with this city. | Hot under #hood#, aye. I'd still rather be hot than caught out. | Three folk told me it's not raining today. I said I'd noticed.
b : You'll cook in that. | That's stubborn. | You did notice, I take it.
a : I'll cook dry, then. #plain.capitalize#. | Stubborn keeps you dry. I'll take it. | I noticed. It'll turn by dusk; #city# always does.

scene evening_rod
when topic=pastimes self.likes=evening_line here.time=dusk
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #rod.capitalize#, after the door's shut. That's my hour, and nobody gets it. | Caught nothing again tonight. Didn't matter. It's the sitting, not the catching, #address#. | Of an evening I carry #rod# to the river. Same spot. Same stone.
b[from=coldwater] #cw : Like the old jetty, near enough. | Sitting's half of it, aye. | Off the jetty, we did that. Every night.
b : Catch much? | Then why bother? | Is it a good spot?
a@cw : Nothing like it. But it'll float. | It's all of it, near enough. #agree.capitalize#. | Every night, still water and a bent pin. I miss it.
a : Two little ones last week. Gave them to a cat. | Because at the river not a soul wants a loaf off me. | #good.capitalize# enough. Nobody else wants it, which makes it the best.

scene summer_light
when topic=season|weather here.season=summer here.time=dusk|night
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : #longevening.capitalize#. I'd stay up till it's gone if I didn't have the door at dawn. | Summer's the only time #city#'s worth walking in, after dark. | Long light tonight. Nothing in the year beats it, and you'll not tell me different.
b : The door can wait an hour. | Only summer? | No argument here.
a : It can't. #queue.capitalize# doesn't. | Only summer. The rest of the year it's #lakedamp# and gulls. | #good.capitalize#. You've sense, then.

scene night_racket
when topic=home self.dislikes=night_noise here.time=dusk|night
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : #racket.capitalize# again last night. Somebody singing a song with no end to it. | I was up at dawn for #almsdoor# and some #fool# was shouting the hour down at midnight. | I asked them nicely to be quiet. Then I asked them less nicely.
b : Did you say anything? | That's hard on you. | And then?
a : I opened the window and told them what I thought of their song. | It's hard on #queue#. I'm sharp with folk on no sleep. | Then they were quiet. #oath#, they were quiet.

scene gulls_roof
when topic=animals self.dislikes=gulls
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : A gull had half a loaf off #bowl# table this morning. In front of sixty hungry folk. | #gulls.capitalize# are the only thing in #city# that steal and nobody minds. | I threw #hood# at a gull once. Missed. Had to go and fetch it off the roof.
b : Cheeky thing. | Fair point. | Off the roof?
a : Cheeky and fat. It's not even #hungry#. | I mind. I mind #very# much. | Off the roof. Never again. Now I throw crusts the other way.

scene south_berth
when topic=dreams|travel
does tell.plan / ask.plan / answer.plan
a : One day I'll get #southship#. Somewhere the sun stays out. | I've asked at the Grayrock office about a berth twice. They laughed. I'll ask a third time. | I want to go somewhere with sun enough #hood# can hang on a peg for a week.
b : And leave the door? | They laughed? | Only a week?
a : Somebody else can hold it. I'd write. #plain.capitalize#. | They did. They'll stop, or I'll stop asking. Not before, #address#. | A week. Then I'd wear it anyway, out of habit.

scene lake_home
when topic=memories self.away=yes self.from=coldwater
does tell.memory / react.self / assess
a : At #self.from_town# #lakedamp# drifted up from the water every evening, soft as a breath. Here it comes in like a slap. | I was raised at #self.from_town#, by the water. Skipped #pebble# off the jetty every night. | Back home nobody went hungry long; you'd knock and somebody'd feed you. I'm trying to make #city# like that.
b[from=coldwater] #cw : Soft lake-damp. I'd forgotten that. | How many skips? | It's not like that here.
b : Do you miss it? | Every night? | That's a big job.
a@cw : I hadn't. Not for a minute. #agree.capitalize#. | Seven, once. Still water helps. | Not yet. Give me time, #address#.
a : #lakedamp.capitalize#, aye. Not much else. | Every night it didn't blow. Calm water and a flat stone. | Big jobs get done one loaf at a time, #address#.

scene lake_words
when topic=accent self.away=yes self.from=coldwater
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I said a thing "won't float" in the queue and somebody asked what I'd floated. | Folk here hear the lake in my voice and think I'm slow. I'm not slow, and I'm not #daft#. | #greet#, I say, and they stare as if I'd spoken to a fish.
b : What had you floated? | Nobody'd think that. | That's a kind sort of hello.
a : Nothing. I said it was #nonsense#, in our words. They got the point. | Some do. They learn otherwise by the second loaf from #bowl#. | It is. #city.capitalize# can get used to it.

scene faith_bread
when topic=faith
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : The Bright One wants folk fed. Everything else in the abbey comes after that. | I pray. Short. The Bright One hears long prayers all day without mine. | A sermon never filled #bowl#. Bread does. I know which I'd rather hand out.
b[job=priest] #priest : There's room for both, you know. | Short prayers are heard too. | We need both, the bread and the word.
b : #bc_fair_enough# | Short's good. | Hard to argue with that.
a@priest : There is. #loaves.capitalize# first, though. Always. | They'd better be. I've not time for long ones. | Both, then. But you'll not see me singing.
a : Fair and true, #address#. | Short and meant. That's the kind I like, #address#. | Then don't argue. #plain.capitalize#.

scene gossip_flat
when topic=gossip
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Somebody in #queue# told me #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I said to go and say it out loud where it can be answered. | I hear #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. If it's true, it'll keep, #address#. If it's not, it shouldn't be said. | Door-talk today: #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I don't pass it on. There. I just did.
b : Did they? | Fair enough. | You did, a bit.
a : Never. Talk like that never goes where it can be answered. That's how you know. | It's the only rule for talk worth having. | I did. That's the last of it. #annoyed#.

scene lean_door
when topic=times world.times=hard|lean
does tell.worry / reassure / assess
a : Lean times. #queue.capitalize#'s twice as long and #loaves# are the same. | Hard winter coming. I've started cutting #loaves# thinner. I hate it. | More folk at #almsdoor# that I've never seen before. Decent folk. Ashamed.
b : You'll manage. You always do. | You've no choice. | They shouldn't be ashamed.
a : I'll manage. Doesn't mean I'll like it. #annoyed#. | No. I still hate it. #plain.capitalize#. | I tell them that. They're ashamed anyway.

scene good_door
when topic=times world.times=good|boom
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Good times. Only twenty in #queue# this morning. I nearly danced. | Coin about, and #poorbox#'s heavier than it's been all year. | Fewer folk need bread. That's the best news there is, and nobody writes it down.
b : Nearly? | Somebody's feeling generous. | You could write it down.
a : Nearly. I don't dance. #oath#, I was tempted. | Somebody is. I'll not ask who. | I did. In #almsbook#, in big letters.

scene learning_trade
when topic=work self.apprentice=yes self.working=yes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Still learning. #self.trade_words.capitalize#. Mostly I'm learning not to say what I think. | They're teaching me #almsbook# and patience. I'm better at the book. | My teacher says I've the heart for it and the temper of a wet cat.
b : That's the hard part. | Patience comes. | Is that fair?
a : It's the only hard part. The rest is counting #loaves#. | It'll have to. I'm not getting any sweeter. | It's fair. I've never been called sweet. #plain.capitalize#.

scene straw_room
when topic=home self.likes=fresh_straw
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Put #straw# down in my room today. Smells like a barn. Best smell there is. | I'd give up most things before I'd give up #straw# on the floor. | New straw, clean floor, #hood# on its peg. That's a home, near enough.
b : It does smell good. | Most things? | Near enough is plenty.
a : It does. Dry and clean. #agree.capitalize#. | Most. Not #rod#. Not #hood#. | It's plenty for me. I'm not fussy, #address#.

scene newcomer_door
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : New face at #almsdoor# today. Didn't want bread, only directions to the Commons. Gave both. | Newcomers always come to #almsdoor# first. #good.capitalize#. That's what it's for. | Somebody new in the street. I'll see them at the door within the month, I'd bet.
b : Both? | Is it, though? | That's a bit grim.
a : Both. Nobody walks far #hungry#. | It is. Ask anyone who's been new. #plain.capitalize#. | It's not grim, it's true. I'll be glad to see them.

story the_hood_story [topic=memories]
  : Little as a #child#, I got caught on the lake shore in a storm with nothing on my head.
  : My gran sewed me #hood# that week, out of an old boat cover. I've worn one ever since.
  ask : Have you got something you'd never go out without?
  b[stage=young|adolescent] : My lucky stone. It's in my pocket now.
  b : My boots, I suppose. Was it this same hood?
  : Pieces of it. Patched so often I couldn't tell you which bits are hers now.

story first_catch [topic=pastimes|memories]
  : The first fish I ever caught, I was so pleased I fell off the jetty with it.
  : Came up still holding the line, and the fish still on it.
  ask : What would you have let go of first, the line or your breath?
  b : The line, I'd think. Did you keep the fish?
  : Ate it that night. Best #supper# I've had, and me dripping on the floor.

story two_hats [topic=work|memories self.working=yes self.job=none]
  : One morning a wolf came to the door in a brown hat and took a loaf.
  : An hour later the same wolf was back in a green hat, holding out a paw.
  ask : Would you have given the second loaf?
  b : Not me. I'd be cross. Did you?
  : Gave a second loaf, and told them the brown suited better. Next morning they turned up bareheaded.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. Out with it. | #greet#, #address#. What do you need?
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #greet#, #topic.player#. Back again. | #topic.player#. Get a hood yet? No. I can see.
dlg @3 resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : Say it straight or don't say it, #address#. | #greet#. I've no time for trouble, #address#.
dlg @1 resident.job : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. I do it properly or not at all. | #self.trade_words.capitalize#. Long days, and worth them.
dlg @2 resident.job [self.working=yes self.job=none] : Bread at #almsdoor#, names in #almsbook#, and no fuss. | I feed folk. Somebody's got to, and it may as well be me.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. Get a hood. | #farewell#, #address#.
graft resident.hub
choice Why do you always wear that hood? -> hood
node hood
say Because it rains. And when it doesn't, it's about to. My gran sewed the first one. I've worn one every day since.
mood calm
free
choice Every day? -> everyday
choice Back to what I asked. -> hub
node everyday
say Every day. Sun, snow, the lot. Laugh if you like. I'll be dry.
mood stern
choice Fair enough. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
